  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a deceased person. The tax is calculated at a flat rate of 6% on the net estate value that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are exempt from estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estates valued over ₱5,000,000, the estate tax liability will be 6% of the amount exceeding this threshold. For example, if an estate is valued at ₱10,000,000, the taxable amount would be ₱5,000,000 (₱10,000,000 - ₱5,000,000), resulting in an estate tax of ₱300,000 (6% of ₱5,000,000). This simplified tax structure aims to streamline the estate tax process and reduce the burden on smaller estates.",
